{"name":"Meatball Red","hex":"#e4002b","fetched":"2026-10-22","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"meatball","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ball of minced or ground meat, seasoned and cooked.","A stupid person; a meathead."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meatball"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the colour which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive colour.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Meatball","blocks":[{"text":"A meatball is ground meat (mince) rolled into a large somewhat spherical ball, sometimes along with other ingredients, such as bread crumbs, minced onion, eggs, butter, and seasoning. Meatballs are cooked by frying, baking, steaming, or braising in sauce. There are many types of meatballs made with different meats and spices. The term is sometimes extended to meatless versions based on legumes, vegetables, mushrooms, fish or other seafood."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Soup_with_meatballs-01.jpg/330px-Soup_with_meatballs-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meatball","wikidata":"Q4831844"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Soup_with_meatballs-01.jpg/500px-Soup_with_meatballs-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Soup_with_meatballs-01.jpg/500px-Soup_with_meatballs-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hochzeitssuppe, a traditional German wedding soup with meatballs","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASoup_with_meatballs-01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Meatballs_on_a_plate.jpg/500px-Meatballs_on_a_plate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Meatballs_on_a_plate.jpg/1280px-Meatballs_on_a_plate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Meatballs_on_a_plate.jpg/500px-Meatballs_on_a_plate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Raw meatballs","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMeatballs_on_a_plate.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Gehaktballetjes.jpg/500px-Gehaktballetjes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Gehaktballetjes.jpg/500px-Gehaktballetjes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail",